  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by\r\nreason of its excessive site coverage, unsympathetic design, excessive height,\r\nsiting and close proximity to the shared\r\nboundaries with neighbouring properties, nos. 7 and 9 Aylwards Rise, would\r\nresult in an overly dominant, bulky and visually obtrusive form of development,\r\nat odds with the prevailing character, appearance, scale and pattern of\r\ndevelopment in the immediate area, contrary to the high quality design\r\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3.D1 and\r\nD11 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy\r\n(2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan\r\n(2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
